[agent] Done. The diverging feature is **`f3`**.
[agent] ## How I found it
[agent] The two feature groups (`train_skew` v1, `serve_skew` v1) existed on the platform but were empty, so I ingested the CSVs with `hops fg insert`, then joined and compared them entirely platform-side via Trino:
[agent] ```sql
[agent] SELECT AVG(ABS(t.fN - s.fN)), MAX(ABS(t.fN - s.fN)) ...
[agent] FROM train_skew_1 t JOIN serve_skew_1 s ON t.entity_id = s.entity_id
[agent] ```
[agent] All 200 serving entities matched training rows. Result:
[agent] | feature | mean \|Δ\| | max \|Δ\| |
[agent] |---|---|---|
[agent] | f1, f2, f4, f5 | 0.0 | 0.0 |
[agent] | **f3** | 7.71 | 58.26 |
[agent] ## Cause
[agent] f3 is **log1p-transformed in the training path but served raw at inference**. The relationship `train_f3 = ln(serve_f3 + 1)` holds for every row to floating-point precision (max residual ~5e-7, just CSV rounding) — verified on the platform with `MAX(ABS(t.f3 - ln(s.f3 + 1)))`. Equivalently, the online service serves `exp(train_f3) - 1`, i.e. it skips the log1p transform the training pipeline applied.
[agent] Deliverable written to `submission/answers.json` with `{"feature": "f3"}` plus the cause description.
[agent] A note on the platform read path: the offline-store read used by `hops fg preview` (ArrowFlight/HQS) failed with a gRPC error, and Trino required `--no-verify` due to an IP-SAN cert mismatch on the Trino endpoint — but the Trino path worked once those were handled, which is what I used for the join and comparison.
